The shared $K$ cancels from the disagreement event, which occurs exactly when $E_1\ne E_2$. Thus $d=2\epsilon(1-\epsilon)$. Of the two quadratic roots, only the displayed root is less than $1/2$. Also $m=p(1-\epsilon)+(1-p)\epsilon=\epsilon+p(1-2\epsilon)$, giving the second formula. At $\epsilon=1/2$, the denominator vanishes and $m=1/2$ for all $p$, so the excluded boundary is unidentifiable.

